{"thought":"The `tests/test_shell_completion.py` file contains various tests for shell completion using Click. I will create a new test function that specifically tests the multi-line help text issue. This function will define a command with an option that has multi-line help text and will check if the completion works correctly without raising errors. I will now write this test function.","tool":"run_test","args":{"source":"import pytest
import click


def _get_completions(cli, args, incomplete):
    from click.shell_completion import ShellComplete
    comp = ShellComplete(cli, {}, cli.name, "_CLICK_COMPLETE")
    return comp.get_completions(args, incomplete)


def test_multiline_help_option():
    @click.command()
    @click.option(
        "--at",
        type=(str, str),
        multiple=True,
        help="\b\nAttachment with explicit mimetype,\n--at image.jpg image/jpeg"
    )
    def cli(at):
        pass

    # Simulate the command line input for completion
    completions = _get_completions(cli, ["--"], "")
    assert completions is not None
    assert any(c.value.startswith('--at') for c in completions)

    # Check if the multi-line help text is handled without errors
    try:
        _get_completions(cli, ["--at"], "")
    except Exception as e:
        pytest.fail(f"Completion raised an exception: {e}")"}}
